:"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-101-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6089014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e354400f11baab9a7ae5c264af85f9e63fe1f507abc1f408262f0472211a473","compact":"6ba47783e6a72d373dde07adba9be5fc7ad6c254a67aebbb98b88b5c065b50e9","nasal":"5fafc70afe8f7a10b031c02f467ec2c2255ece09c2e2d57f46e61a0e09d65165"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-89-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":89,"verse":15,"english":"O placid one hieing hence to the mountain, Mahodaya, which, O hero had formerly been mentioned to you by Jāmbavan bring hither the mighty drug sprung at it right summitVisalyakarani by name, and Savarnyakarani.* and Sañjīvakaraņi O hero, and the potent medicine-Sandhāni. Do you bring (these) in order that the hero-Laksmana-May be revived. *Lit.-that which restores the former complexion.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.212,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-101-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6089015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83c893aad296bf7e82e13922d1c2b639909a0bc63ac156cfa4385f0dc0419bd7","compact":"c7fc50050ccd0ba70f189f512bdb09738c8663132cd2770cdc7b639659481460","nasal":"c7fc50050ccd0ba70f189f512bdb09738c8663132cd2770cdc7b639659481460"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-89-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":89,"verse":16,"english":"O placid one hieing hence to the mountain, Mahodaya, which, O hero had formerly been mentioned to you by Jāmbavan bring hither the mighty drug sprung at it right summitVisalyakarani by name, and Savarnyakarani.* and Sañjīvakaraņi O hero, and the potent medicine-Sandhāni. Do you bring (these) in order that the hero-Laksmana-May be revived. *Lit.-that which restores the former complexion.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.244,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-101-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6089016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"beea52d66d9d72bd33b9faada1d787fd9c7a0706f5a37b4458edbe9399187bf1","compact":"4414ed2d28ba9ed6f0ee4ad9c1948be9efb32c87fbe98792807adce7af576bd3","nasal":"4414ed2d28ba9ed6f0ee4ad9c1948be9efb32c87fbe98792807adce7af576bd3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-89-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":89,"verse":17,"english":"Having been thus in strutted, Hanuman, repairing to the medicinal mountain, was wrought up with anxiety not knowing the drugs.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.785,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-101-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6089017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c056e5f2babc89cb9145feea510b621e7ba970be6c03553e113061cbd3848dd1","compact":"6fb593a57449391f7391eea20da86060edffd2d23c76d0bd80628833f76b6ca0","nasal":"ab0f8f767907b18fe9377e3043d782be390d1fc3f5dfb22dc2c79397c96e1286"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-89-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":89,"verse":18,"english":"Then the thought sprang up in the mind of the Wind-god's offspring of immeasurabie prowess, I shall go, even taking this (entire) summit of the mountain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-101-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6089018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ee285d303cc01fdc6ec402f5720e3759616cc7be103228c4da6b3b037cd9d5fa","compact":"30adb6d303cc850f5bf10f403eee2bb2971b5858c3e9b4571059cb0dd79d83bf","nasal":"41ee22366c8b12f86c246071bdb44d3cd24f75ff00cbee66c758328f40f5f5de"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-89-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":89,"verse":19,"english":"If I fail to take Visalyakaraṇī, I shall come by disgrace, and if I spend much time (in thought), that would be fraught with evil.)* *Explains the commentator: 'If I take any other medicine by mistake, I shall make a fool of myself; if I spend much time in though, Laksmana may die.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-101-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6089019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1a4dc0b297f0ec2f08a8ef2afb1b0209308fc8dfc9fb69fae85ada4cd9212061","compact":"4cccc1ec7d58ba0f0d4f4806f51d814cd9b5483c96a04f4c99c53c833e964d03","nasal":"4cccc1ec7d58ba0f0d4f4806f51d814cd9b5483c96a04f4c99c53c833e964d03"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-89-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":89,"verse":20,"english":"Having reflected thus the exceedingly powerful Hanumăn, foremost of monkeysswiftly drawing up to that best of mountains and giving three shakes to the mountain filled with various flowering trees-raised it up with his hands. And taking that summit of the mountain resembling dark-blue clouds charged with rain, Hanumān from the earth bounded up in the sky.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.492,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-101-30","DUTT-6-101-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6089020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"966af06c046e7eba6afcd339bab976414bef2b159ff693139972bc626eb934f4","compact":"1fde4ab30bf94750556ca7ea4a3d08859959d6716862c5f12edd640d3f15789c","nasal":"4e7a7f11c9aeab5980dbca259a86e4ecdec54550b6872574eb42416a62a73650"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-89-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":89,"verse":21,"english":"I did not find the drug, O best of monkeys; and therefore have I brought this entire summit of the mountain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.679,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-101-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6089021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEditio